12.76 emacsvox-extras
=====================

Infrequently used wizards archived for posterity.

12.76.1 Emacsvox-Extras Commands
--------------------------------

12.76.1.1 emacsvox-annotate-add-annotation
..........................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-annotate-add-annotation (&optional reset)

     Add annotation to the annotation working buffer.
     Prompt for annotation buffer if not already set.
     Interactive prefix arg ‘reset’ prompts for the annotation
     buffer even if one is already set.
     Annotation is entered in a temporary buffer and the
     annotation is inserted into the working buffer when complete.

     (fn &optional RESET)

12.76.1.2 emacsvox-clipfile-copy
................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-clipfile-copy (start end &optional prompt)
     ‘C-e C-M-c’

     Use file-based Emacsvox Clipboard --
     dis a convenient way of sharing information between independent
     Emacsvox sessions running on  different machines.

     (fn START END &optional PROMPT)

12.76.1.3 emacsvox-clipfile-paste
.................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-clipfile-paste (&optional paste-table)

     Yank contents of the Emacsvox clipboard at point.

     (fn &optional PASTE-TABLE)

12.76.1.4 emacsvox-curl
.......................

 -- Command: emacsvox-curl (url)

     Grab URL using Curl, and preview it with a browser .

     (fn URL)

12.76.1.5 emacsvox-wizards-add-autoload-cookies
...............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-add-autoload-cookies (&optional f)

     Add autoload cookies to file f.
     Default is to add autoload cookies to current file.

     (fn &optional F)

12.76.1.6 emacsvox-wizards-bindings-from-org
............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-bindings-from-org (variable filename)

     Load bindings from a specified file.

     (fn VARIABLE FILENAME)

12.76.1.7 emacsvox-wizards-bindings-to-org
..........................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-bindings-to-org (variable filename)

     Persists mapping to org file.

     (fn VARIABLE FILENAME)

12.76.1.8 emacsvox-wizards-display-pod-as-manpage
.................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-display-pod-as-manpage (filename)

     Create a virtual manpage in Emacs from the Perl Online Documentation.

     (fn FILENAME)

12.76.1.9 emacsvox-wizards-find-grep
....................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-find-grep (glob pattern)

     Run compile using find and grep.
     Interactive  arguments specify filename pattern and search pattern.

     (fn GLOB PATTERN)

12.76.1.10 emacsvox-wizards-fix-read-only-text
..............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-fix-read-only-text (start end)

     Nuke read-only property on text range.

     (fn START END)

12.76.1.11 emacsvox-wizards-generate-voice-sampler
..................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-generate-voice-sampler (step)

     Generate a buffer that shows a sample line in all the ACSS settings
     for the current voice family.

     (fn STEP)

12.76.1.12 emacsvox-wizards-list-voices
.......................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-list-voices (pattern)
     ‘C-h "’
     ‘<f1> "’
     ‘<help> "’

     Show all defined voice-face mappings  in a help buffer.
     Sample text to use comes from variable
       ‘ems-wizards-sampler-text

     (fn PATTERN)

12.76.1.13 emacsvox-wizards-midi-using-m-score
..............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-midi-using-m-score (midi-file)

     Play midi file using mscore from musescore package.

     (fn MIDI-FILE)

12.76.1.14 emacsvox-wizards-show-voices
.......................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-show-voices

     Display a buffer with sample text in the defined voices.

12.76.1.15 emacsvox-wizards-voice-sampler
.........................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-wizards-voice-sampler (personality)

     Read a personality  and apply it to the current line.

     (fn PERSONALITY)

12.76.2 emacsvox-extras Options
-------------------------------

 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-clipfile-file
     File used to save Emacsvox clipboard.
     The emacsvox clipboard provides a convenient mechanism for exchanging
     information between different Emacs sessions.

     Default Value:

     "/home/bart/.emacsvox//clipboard"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-curl-cookie-store
     Cookie store used by Curl.

     Default Value:

     "/home/bart/.curl-cookies"



