12.91 emacsvox-gnus
===================

This module advises gnus to speak.  Updating support in 2014 (Emacsvox
is nearly 20 years old) Updating in 2018 as I switch to gnus as my
primary mail interface.  These customizations to gnus make it convenient
to listen to news: You can read news mostly by using the four arrow
keys.  By default all article headers are hidden, so you hear the real
news.

12.91.1 Emacsvox-Gnus Commands
------------------------------

12.91.1.1 emacsvox-gnus-personal-gmail-last-week
................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-gnus-personal-gmail-last-week

     Look for mail addressed personally in the last week.

12.91.1.2 emacsvox-gnus-personal-gmail-recent
.............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-gnus-personal-gmail-recent

     Look for mail addressed personally in the last day.

12.91.1.3 emacsvox-gnus-summary-catchup-quietly-and-exit
........................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-gnus-summary-catchup-quietly-and-exit

     Catch up on all articles in current group.

12.91.2 emacsvox-gnus Options
-----------------------------

 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-gnus-large-article
     Articles having more than
     emacsvox-gnus-large-article lines will be considered to be a large article.
     A large article is not spoken all at once;
     instead you hear only the first screenful.

     Default Value:

     100


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-gnus-punctuation-mode
     Pronunciation mode to use for gnus buffers.

     Default Value:

     all



